Task 1: Request and Deploy Service Certificates
Subtask 1.1: Prepare the Certificate Request Environment
First, let's set up our environment and understand the current certificate status.

Connect to the IdM server:
ssh root@idm-server
Verify IdM server status:
ipactl status
Authenticate as IdM administrator:
kinit admin
Check current certificates:
ipa cert-find --all
Subtask 1.2: Generate Certificate Signing Request (CSR)
Now we'll create a certificate signing request for our web service.

Create a directory for certificate operations:
mkdir -p /etc/ssl/certs/lab15
cd /etc/ssl/certs/lab15
Generate a private key for the web service:
openssl genrsa -out webservice.key 2048
Set proper permissions on the private key:
chmod 600 webservice.key
Create a certificate signing request:
openssl req -new -key webservice.key -out webservice.csr -subj "/CN=web-server.example.com/O=Example Organization/C=US"
Verify the CSR content:
openssl req -in webservice.csr -text -noout
Subtask 1.3: Request Certificate from IdM CA
Submit the certificate request to IdM:
ipa cert-request webservice.csr --principal=HTTP/web-server.example.com
Note the certificate serial number from the output and store it:
CERT_SERIAL=$(ipa cert-request webservice.csr --principal=HTTP/web-server.example.com | grep "Serial number:" | awk '{print $3}')
echo "Certificate Serial: $CERT_SERIAL"
Retrieve the issued certificate:
ipa cert-show $CERT_SERIAL --out=webservice.crt
Verify the certificate details:
openssl x509 -in webservice.crt -text -noout
Subtask 1.4: Create Certificate Chain
Get the CA certificate:
ipa ca-show ipa --certificate-out=ca.crt
Create a full certificate chain:
cat webservice.crt ca.crt > webservice-chain.crt
Verify the certificate chain:
openssl verify -CAfile ca.crt webservice.crt
Task 2: Configure Services to Use Issued Certificates
Subtask 2.1: Configure HTTPD Service
Let's configure Apache HTTPD to use our newly issued certificate.

Connect to the web server:
ssh root@web-server
Install required packages:
dnf install -y httpd mod_ssl
Copy certificates to the web server (from idm-server):
# On idm-server, copy files to web-server
scp /etc/ssl/certs/lab15/webservice.key root@web-server:/etc/ssl/private/
scp /etc/ssl/certs/lab15/webservice-chain.crt root@web-server:/etc/ssl/certs/
scp /etc/ssl/certs/lab15/ca.crt root@web-server:/etc/ssl/certs/
Set proper permissions on web server:
chmod 600 /etc/ssl/private/webservice.key
chmod 644 /etc/ssl/certs/webservice-chain.crt
chmod 644 /etc/ssl/certs/ca.crt
Configure SSL virtual host:
cat > /etc/httpd/conf.d/ssl-lab15.conf << 'EOF'
<VirtualHost *:443>
    ServerName web-server.example.com
    DocumentRoot /var/www/html
    
    SSLEngine on
    SSLCertificateFile /etc/ssl/certs/webservice-chain.crt
    SSLCertificateKeyFile /etc/ssl/private/webservice.key
    SSLCACertificateFile /etc/ssl/certs/ca.crt
    
    # Modern SSL configuration
    SSLProtocol all -SSLv3 -TLSv1 -TLSv1.1
    SSLCipherSuite ECDHE-ECDSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-ECDSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384:ECDHE-RSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384
    SSLHonorCipherOrder off
    SSLSessionTickets off
    
    # Security headers
    Header always set Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload"
    Header always set X-Frame-Options DENY
    Header always set X-Content-Type-Options nosniff
</VirtualHost>
EOF
Create a test page:
cat > /var/www/html/index.html << 'EOF'
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>IdM Certificate Lab</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>SSL Certificate Test Page</h1>
    <p>This page is served using an IdM-issued certificate.</p>
    <p>Server: web-server.example.com</p>
</body>
</html>
EOF
Enable and start HTTPD:
systemctl enable httpd
systemctl start httpd
Open firewall ports:
firewall-cmd --permanent --add-service=http
firewall-cmd --permanent --add-service=https
firewall-cmd --reload
Subtask 2.2: Configure LDAP Service with Certificates
Now let's configure LDAP to use certificates for secure connections.

Return to the IdM server:
ssh root@idm-server
Create LDAP service certificate request:
cd /etc/ssl/certs/lab15
openssl genrsa -out ldapservice.key 2048
chmod 600 ldapservice.key
Generate CSR for LDAP service:
openssl req -new -key ldapservice.key -out ldapservice.csr -subj "/CN=idm-server.example.com/O=Example Organization/C=US"
Request certificate for LDAP service:
LDAP_CERT_SERIAL=$(ipa cert-request ldapservice.csr --principal=ldap/idm-server.example.com | grep "Serial number:" | awk '{print $3}')
echo "LDAP Certificate Serial: $LDAP_CERT_SERIAL"
Retrieve the LDAP certificate:
ipa cert-show $LDAP_CERT_SERIAL --out=ldapservice.crt
Create LDAP certificate chain:
cat ldapservice.crt ca.crt > ldapservice-chain.crt
Copy certificates to LDAP directory:
cp ldapservice.key /etc/dirsrv/slapd-EXAMPLE-COM/
cp ldapservice-chain.crt /etc/dirsrv/slapd-EXAMPLE-COM/
chown dirsrv:dirsrv /etc/dirsrv/slapd-EXAMPLE-COM/ldapservice.*
chmod 600 /etc/dirsrv/slapd-EXAMPLE-COM/ldapservice.key
Subtask 2.3: Test Certificate Deployment
Test HTTPS connection:
curl -k https://web-server.example.com
Test certificate validation:
openssl s_client -connect web-server.example.com:443 -CAfile /etc/ssl/certs/lab15/ca.crt
Check certificate expiration:
echo | openssl s_client -connect web-server.example.com:443 2>/dev/null | openssl x509 -noout -dates
Task 3: Automate Certificate Deployment
Subtask 3.1: Create Certificate Request Script
Let's create a script to automate the certificate request process.

Create automation directory:
mkdir -p /opt/cert-automation
cd /opt/cert-automation
Create certificate request script:
cat > request-service-cert.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

# Certificate Request Automation Script
# Usage: ./request-service-cert.sh <service-name> <hostname> <principal>

set -e

SERVICE_NAME="$1"
HOSTNAME="$2"
PRINCIPAL="$3"

if [ $# -ne 3 ]; then
    echo "Usage: $0 <service-name> <hostname> <principal>"
    echo "Example: $0 webservice web-server.example.com HTTP/web-server.example.com"
    exit 1
fi

CERT_DIR="/etc/ssl/certs/automated"
mkdir -p "$CERT_DIR"
cd "$CERT_DIR"

echo "Generating private key for $SERVICE_NAME..."
openssl genrsa -out "${SERVICE_NAME}.key" 2048
chmod 600 "${SERVICE_NAME}.key"

echo "Creating certificate signing request..."
openssl req -new -key "${SERVICE_NAME}.key" -out "${SERVICE_NAME}.csr" \
    -subj "/CN=${HOSTNAME}/O=Example Organization/C=US"

echo "Requesting certificate from IdM CA..."
CERT_SERIAL=$(ipa cert-request "${SERVICE_NAME}.csr" --principal="$PRINCIPAL" | \
    grep "Serial number:" | awk '{print $3}')

if [ -z "$CERT_SERIAL" ]; then
    echo "Error: Failed to get certificate serial number"
    exit 1
fi

echo "Certificate serial number: $CERT_SERIAL"

echo "Retrieving issued certificate..."
ipa cert-show "$CERT_SERIAL" --out="${SERVICE_NAME}.crt"

echo "Getting CA certificate..."
ipa ca-show ipa --certificate-out=ca.crt

echo "Creating certificate chain..."
cat "${SERVICE_NAME}.crt" ca.crt > "${SERVICE_NAME}-chain.crt"

echo "Verifying certificate..."
openssl verify -CAfile ca.crt "${SERVICE_NAME}.crt"

echo "Certificate files created:"
echo "  Private key: ${CERT_DIR}/${SERVICE_NAME}.key"
echo "  Certificate: ${CERT_DIR}/${SERVICE_NAME}.crt"
echo "  Chain: ${CERT_DIR}/${SERVICE_NAME}-chain.crt"
echo "  CA: ${CERT_DIR}/ca.crt"

# Store certificate info
cat > "${SERVICE_NAME}-info.txt" << INFO
Service: $SERVICE_NAME
Hostname: $HOSTNAME
Principal: $PRINCIPAL
Serial: $CERT_SERIAL
Created: $(date)
Expires: $(openssl x509 -in "${SERVICE_NAME}.crt" -noout -enddate | cut -d= -f2)
INFO

echo "Certificate request completed successfully!"
EOF
Make the script executable:
chmod +x request-service-cert.sh
Subtask 3.2: Create Certificate Deployment Script
Create deployment script:
cat > deploy-service-cert.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

# Certificate Deployment Automation Script
# Usage: ./deploy-service-cert.sh <service-name> <target-host> <service-type>

set -e

SERVICE_NAME="$1"
TARGET_HOST="$2"
SERVICE_TYPE="$3"

if [ $# -ne 3 ]; then
    echo "Usage: $0 <service-name> <target-host> <service-type>"
    echo "Service types: httpd, nginx, ldap"
    echo "Example: $0 webservice web-server.example.com httpd"
    exit 1
fi

CERT_DIR="/etc/ssl/certs/automated"
REMOTE_CERT_DIR="/etc/ssl/certs"
REMOTE_KEY_DIR="/etc/ssl/private"

if [ ! -f "${CERT_DIR}/${SERVICE_NAME}.key" ]; then
    echo "Error: Certificate files not found for $SERVICE_NAME"
    echo "Run request-service-cert.sh first"
    exit 1
fi

echo "Deploying certificates for $SERVICE_NAME to $TARGET_HOST..."

# Copy certificates to target host
echo "Copying certificate files..."
ssh root@"$TARGET_HOST" "mkdir -p $REMOTE_CERT_DIR $REMOTE_KEY_DIR"

scp "${CERT_DIR}/${SERVICE_NAME}.key" root@"$TARGET_HOST":"$REMOTE_KEY_DIR/"
scp "${CERT_DIR}/${SERVICE_NAME}-chain.crt" root@"$TARGET_HOST":"$REMOTE_CERT_DIR/"
scp "${CERT_DIR}/ca.crt" root@"$TARGET_HOST":"$REMOTE_CERT_DIR/"

# Set permissions
ssh root@"$TARGET_HOST" "chmod 600 $REMOTE_KEY_DIR/${SERVICE_NAME}.key"
ssh root@"$TARGET_HOST" "chmod 644 $REMOTE_CERT_DIR/${SERVICE_NAME}-chain.crt"
ssh root@"$TARGET_HOST" "chmod 644 $REMOTE_CERT_DIR/ca.crt"

# Configure service based on type
case "$SERVICE_TYPE" in
    httpd)
        echo "Configuring Apache HTTPD..."
        ssh root@"$TARGET_HOST" << HTTPD_CONFIG
cat > /etc/httpd/conf.d/ssl-${SERVICE_NAME}.conf << 'HTTPD_EOF'
<VirtualHost *:443>
    ServerName ${TARGET_HOST}
    DocumentRoot /var/www/html
    
    SSLEngine on
    SSLCertificateFile ${REMOTE_CERT_DIR}/${SERVICE_NAME}-chain.crt
    SSLCertificateKeyFile ${REMOTE_KEY_DIR}/${SERVICE_NAME}.key
    SSLCACertificateFile ${REMOTE_CERT_DIR}/ca.crt
    
    SSLProtocol all -SSLv3 -TLSv1 -TLSv1.1
    SSLCipherSuite ECDHE-ECDSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256
    SSLHonorCipherOrder off
</VirtualHost>
HTTPD_EOF

systemctl reload httpd
HTTPD_CONFIG
        ;;
    nginx)
        echo "Configuring Nginx..."
        ssh root@"$TARGET_HOST" << NGINX_CONFIG
cat > /etc/nginx/conf.d/ssl-${SERVICE_NAME}.conf << 'NGINX_EOF'
server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name ${TARGET_HOST};
    
    ssl_certificate ${REMOTE_CERT_DIR}/${SERVICE_NAME}-chain.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key ${REMOTE_KEY_DIR}/${SERVICE_NAME}.key;
    ssl_trusted_certificate ${REMOTE_CERT_DIR}/ca.crt;
    
    ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
    ssl_ciphers ECDHE-ECDSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256;
    
    location / {
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;
        index index.html;
    }
}
NGINX_EOF

systemctl reload nginx
NGINX_CONFIG
        ;;
    *)
        echo "Service type $SERVICE_TYPE not supported in this script"
        echo "Certificates deployed but service not configured"
        ;;
esac

echo "Certificate deployment completed for $SERVICE_NAME on $TARGET_HOST"
EOF
Make the deployment script executable:
chmod +x deploy-service-cert.sh
Subtask 3.3: Create Certificate Monitoring Script
Create monitoring script:
cat > monitor-certificates.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

# Certificate Monitoring Script
# Checks certificate expiration and validity

CERT_DIR="/etc/ssl/certs/automated"
WARNING_DAYS=30

echo "Certificate Monitoring Report - $(date)"
echo "========================================"

if [ ! -d "$CERT_DIR" ]; then
    echo "No certificates found in $CERT_DIR"
    exit 0
fi

cd "$CERT_DIR"

for cert_file in *.crt; do
    if [ -f "$cert_file" ]; then
        echo ""
        echo "Certificate: $cert_file"
        echo "-------------------"
        
        # Get certificate details
        SUBJECT=$(openssl x509 -in "$cert_file" -noout -subject | sed 's/subject=//')
        ISSUER=$(openssl x509 -in "$cert_file" -noout -issuer | sed 's/issuer=//')
        NOT_AFTER=$(openssl x509 -in "$cert_file" -noout -enddate | cut -d= -f2)
        
        echo "Subject: $SUBJECT"
        echo "Issuer: $ISSUER"
        echo "Expires: $NOT_AFTER"
        
        # Check expiration
        EXPIRE_DATE=$(date -d "$NOT_AFTER" +%s)
        CURRENT_DATE=$(date +%s)
        DAYS_UNTIL_EXPIRE=$(( (EXPIRE_DATE - CURRENT_DATE) / 86400 ))
        
        if [ $DAYS_UNTIL_EXPIRE -lt 0 ]; then
            echo "Status: EXPIRED ($((0 - DAYS_UNTIL_EXPIRE)) days ago)"
        elif [ $DAYS_UNTIL_EXPIRE -lt $WARNING_DAYS ]; then
            echo "Status: WARNING (expires in $DAYS_UNTIL_EXPIRE days)"
        else
            echo "Status: OK (expires in $DAYS_UNTIL_EXPIRE days)"
        fi
        
        # Verify certificate
        if openssl verify -CAfile ca.crt "$cert_file" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
            echo "Verification: VALID"
        else
            echo "Verification: INVALID"
        fi
    fi
done

echo ""
echo "Monitoring complete."
EOF
Make the monitoring script executable:
chmod +x monitor-certificates.sh
